<!--
  A stipulation, not a filing. See assets/fixtures/README.md.

  The construction a third party actually performs, end to end: bring their layer in, make one
  of your own beside it, make a third layer out of both, and keep all three apart afterwards.

    as-filed        one part, foreign     the bakery's oven line, carried through unchanged
    as-contracted   no part, originated   the same line, read a second way
    both-views      two parts, local      made out of the two above

  The third fusion is possible because a filing can say which filing it is. A part whose
  notation matches this document's own is a local part. There is no second kind of part and no
  new element on `asrt:Part`: the difference is a comparison of two strings.

  A layer made out of two views of one quantity is an ordinary fusion with an elimination, not
  a new relation. Added together, two views of one quantity count it twice, which is what
  `Elimination` removes; an elimination against `demand` is what was asked, counted twice.

    demand      the parts add up to 3600, 4000 and 4800; less the 1800, 2000 and 2400
                eliminated, the composed demand is 1800, 2000 and 2400
    nameplate   the parts add up to 4320; less the 2160 eliminated, the composed nameplate
                is 2160

  The eliminated copy is the whole range, not a single value. An elimination comes off bound by
  bound, because what it removes is part of the very figure it comes off, and for two views of
  one quantity that holds exactly: the removed copy is the figure, so it moves with it at every
  bound.

  The sum rule stays exact through it. A checker owes the same arithmetic here as for any other
  fusion; nothing is suspended and nothing is treated specially. That is the test of whether
  composition was the right answer: had it needed the rule relaxed, it would not have been.

  The two views are two layers, though their figures are identical and each files one
  `customer` holder with an unmeasured share: they read the same line two ways, as the bakery
  filed it and as contracted capacity. Nobody is wrong, and nothing was corrected.
-->
